# **Slide 19 — useEffect Cleanup & Dependency**

### 📖 Theory
- Effects can return a **cleanup function** → removes subscriptions, clears timers, etc.  
- Prevents **memory leaks** when component unmounts.  

👉 Example use-cases:  
- Cleanup event listeners.  
- Stop API polling.  
- Clear intervals.  

### 💻 Small Code
```jsx
import { useEffect } from "react";

function Timer() {
  useEffect(() => {
    const id = setInterval(() => console.log("Tick ⏱️"), 1000);

    return () => clearInterval(id); // cleanup when component unmounts
  }, []);

  return <p>Timer running…</p>;
}

export default Timer;
```

✅ When Timer unmounts → cleanup clears interval.  

